  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy. Image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23), raising the question of whether adding image features to the strong RNA signal will help or merely inject noise. Uncertainty: We have no multimodal result yet, so we cannot tell whether fusion adds complementary information or degrades the RNA signal. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly extends the best RNA configuration by adding the image modality while keeping all other settings (encoder, profile, aggregation) identical to config_005. It isolates the effect of adding image + concat fusion. If accuracy improves over 0.650, it confirms multimodal value and guides further fusion/image-encoder exploration; if it does not, it tells us to focus budget on RNA-only refinements rather than testing all 24 multimodal variants. This is the highest-information single experiment under the limited budget because it answers the central design question (does image help?) with the fewest new variables introduced."
}

